      "writtenOn": "2025-05-15T21:42:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "understood.\nIn the POR implementation, if `reg` is initialized to `0` by default, and then `cros_flash_npcx_get_status_reg` fails without updating `reg` (e.g., due to an underlying communication error during power-on reset), the do-while loop in `cros_flash_npcx_wait_ready` would then evaluate (`reg \u0026 SPI_NOR_WIP_BIT`) as (0 \u0026 1), which is 0. This would cause the loop to break prematurely and falsely indicate that the flash is ready, even though the status read actually failed.",
      "parentUuid": "ea9430cd_f23f1fae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 78,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 78,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "be99b868f7746d3a9521c519bd80eff417730087",
